# Allow-list: the build context holds ONLY what an image needs. Everything else, and above
# all data/ (PPMI and other data under data use agreements) and any .env, never reaches a
# Docker build, so it cannot end up inside an image (CLAUDE.md section 4).
*
!services/backend/
# The voice module's code and package list, so voice analyses run in the container. Its
# tests, notebooks and artifacts (the trained model) stay out: the model is mounted instead.
!models/voice/requirements.txt
!models/voice/src/
models/**/__pycache__
services/backend/**/__pycache__
services/backend/**/*.pyc
services/backend/.env
services/backend/tests/
# Accounts reach the container as a compose secret at run time, never inside the image.
dev-accounts.json
